 =?UTF-8?q?=20transfer's=20executor=20runs=20the=20guest=20ramp?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

display_transfer runs the transfer.comp compute over the two surfaces
(MetalSurface's check_surface loads the input's rows from the guest
honestly — linear rows read linear, tiled ones through the Morton —
and the output mounts at its own address), the push constants carry
the GLSL block's words verbatim (size, input height, output height,
scale, flip, the two formats), and the output's pixels come out the
block averages the shader's own rounding computes: the grey ramp's
16x16 columns 2x-pair averaged to pixel (2x+1) exactly — (0,0)=1,
(7,0)=15, all four channels settled through the decode's ABGR flip.

the Transfer struct moves to raster.rs proper, out of the vulkan-
gated hardware.rs: the shape belongs to the GSP's registers, and the
metal build reads it now. the guest's memory test uses the GpuMemory
trait's own read/write (the fake's write_raw named apart from the
trait's write).

147 gpu tests green with the metal feature, the workspace's paths
clean.
